# Phase 7A -- external dataset (Tobi-Bueck/customer-support-tickets).
# The raw CSVs (~53 MB) and the derived caches are reproducible from the
# pinned revision recorded in data/external_tobibueck/PROVENANCE.json, so the
# REPORT is committed and the bulk data is not. Note that the existing
# data/ticket_embeddings*.npy pattern does not cover this path.
data/external_tobibueck/raw/
data/external_tobibueck/english_subset.csv
data/external_tobibueck/*.npy
data/external_tobibueck/*.npz
data/external_tobibueck/*.faiss

# Paper revision (Oct 2026) -- real-world tickets, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.7648117
# (CC BY 4.0). Same rule as 7A: the raw files and the full English text are
# regenerable from md5-pinned downloads (scripts/fetch_zenodo_tickets.py,
# scripts/prepare_zenodo_tickets.py), so results are committed and bulk text
# is not. See data/external_zenodo_7648117/PROVENANCE.json.
data/external_zenodo_7648117/raw/
data/external_zenodo_7648117/english_tickets.csv

# Aryan's local Overleaf upload copy of paper/ (never committed)
/paper_upload.zip

# Phase 9B: embedding caches anywhere in the tree (none is tracked; the
# path-specific patterns above predate this and are kept)
*.npy
